  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Groww, Played Straight",
    "overview": "This is Groww's own light app with Beginner Mode living inside it. Surfaces are white cards on a near-white ground, separated by hairlines rather than shadows; one sans (Figtree, standing in for the proprietary GrowwSans) carries everything; Groww green is the only brand voice. The guidance (next steps, explanations, charge breakdowns, the F&O lock) is the only new thing, and it arrives in the same quiet materials as the rest of the app, never as a separate visual register.\n\nDensity is Groww's: compact mobile rows, 14px body, big bold ink figures where money is the headline. Tokens come from groww.in's production palette, with text-bearing greens, greys, reds and ambers taken one step darker on Groww's own scale so every text pairing clears WCAG AA. Numbers are always tabular and in Indian format; gain and loss always carry a sign as well as a colour.\n\nThe world rejects the prototype's earlier bespoke forest-and-mint identity and any flourish Groww would not ship.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White bordered cards (12px) on a #F8F8F8 ground; flat, hairline-separated.",
      "One family, Figtree, bold for figures and headings, tabular numerals for every amount.",
      "Two greens with split jobs: brand green for fills, bars, dots and icons; darker green for text and white-label buttons.",
      "Pills only for chips, tags and segmented tabs; 8px for controls.",
      "Lists inside cards are hairline-divided rows, never nested boxes."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Greens Rule",
        "body": "Brand green (#04B488) fills shapes; deep green (#00825C) carries text and white labels. If a green is behind or forming letters, it is the deep one.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Signed Money Rule",
        "body": "Gains render in deep green with \"+\", losses in loss red with the true minus sign \"−\". Colour never carries the meaning alone.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink Returns Rule",
        "body": "Headline values and past-performance return figures are ink; only explicit gain/loss deltas take green or red. Daily moves in dense lists (\"−0.6% today\") stay secondary grey with their sign.",
